  "rule": "Each 5x5 square has a frame of colour 8 or 2 around a 3x3 core of another colour. 8-framed squares slide to the left edge and 2-framed squares slide to the right edge, and every square keeps its rows. Within each frame colour, the square nearest its wall moves first, and later squares stack against row-overlapping squares of the same colour.",
  "scope": "Supported: sampled grid size (width 14-26, height 12-26), background colour from {0,1,3,4,5,6,7,9}, and 3-10 squares (limited by area) at random non-overlapping positions; touching squares are allowed. Frames are 8 or 2. Cores are any colour other than the square's own frame and the background, so a core can be 2 or 8 in the opposite-frame square. Each scene has at least one square of each frame colour, and stacking chains arise naturally. Not supported: frame colours other than 8 and 2, square sizes other than 5x5, and collisions between the left-moving and right-moving groups in the output (such scenes are rejected).",
  "constraints": [
    "Input squares never overlap; they may touch.",
    "Background is never 2 or 8, and a core never equals its own frame or the background.",
    "A row-major 5x5 window scan with used-cell marking must recover exactly the latent squares, so there are no spurious or shifted detections.",
    "Every slid square stays inside the grid.",
    "Slid squares from the two frame groups never overlap in the output.",
    "At least one square changes position (no identity samples).",
    "Both frame colours are present in every random scene."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "The canonical fixtures are all 22x22; the random sampler varies size within 12-26 rows and 14-26 columns.",
